Use `indexOf` + `splice`:

```js
const index = array.indexOf(value);

if (index !== -1) {
  array.splice(index, 1);
}
```

### Example
```js
let array = [1, 2, 3, 4, 3];
let value = 3;

let index = array.indexOf(value);
if (index !== -1) {
  array.splice(index, 1);
}

console.log(array); // [1, 2, 4, 3]
```

### Notes
- `indexOf(value)` finds the first matching item.
- `splice(index, 1)` removes 1 item at that position.
- This changes the original array.

### If you want to remove all matching values
```js
array = array.filter(item => item !== value);
```

Example:
```js
let array = [1, 2, 3, 4, 3];
let value = 3;

array = array.filter(item => item !== value);

console.log(array); // [1, 2, 4]
```

### If you want a reusable helper
```js
function removeItem(arr, value) {
  const index = arr.indexOf(value);
  if (index !== -1) {
    arr.splice(index, 1);
  }
  return arr;
}
```

